! spoke1 — DMVPN Phase 2 spoke  (Arista EOS)
!
! Physical IPs and Tunnel0 base are pre-configured.
! YOUR TASK: Configure NHRP, OSPF broadcast, and ip nhrp shortcut.
!
! -------------------------------------------------------
! Phase 2 spoke configuration:
!
! Step 1 — Configure NHRP and OSPF on Tunnel0:
!   configure
!   interface Tunnel0
!      ip nhrp network-id 1
!      ip nhrp holdtime 300
!      ip nhrp nhs 172.16.0.1 nbma 10.0.0.1 multicast
!      ip nhrp map 172.16.0.1 10.0.0.1
!      ip nhrp shortcut
!      ip ospf network broadcast
!      ip ospf priority 0
!      ip ospf area 0
!
! Step 2 — Configure OSPF process:
!   router ospf 1
!      router-id 10.0.0.11
!      passive-interface Loopback0
!      passive-interface Loopback1
!
! Step 3 — Verify Phase 2 operation:
!   show ip nhrp                    <- hub entry + dynamic spoke entries after shortcut
!   show ip ospf neighbor           <- hub as Full/DR + other spokes as Full/DROTHER
!   show ip route 192.168.2.0       <- next-hop should be 172.16.0.12 (spoke2 direct!)
!   traceroute 192.168.2.1          <- should NOT transit hub after NHRP shortcut resolves
!   ping 192.168.2.1 repeat 100     <- first few packets via hub, then direct spoke-to-spoke
!
! Phase 2 key insight:
!   OSPF broadcast mode: the DR (hub) floods LSAs that carry the ORIGINATING
!   router's tunnel IP as the next-hop.  So spoke1's routing table shows:
!     192.168.2.0/24 via 172.16.0.12  (spoke2 tunnel IP directly, not hub)
!   When spoke1 first sends to 172.16.0.12 it has no NBMA mapping for that IP,
!   so it falls back to NHRP — hub forwards the packet and sends NHRP redirect.
!   spoke1 resolves spoke2 NBMA IP (10.0.0.12) and installs a shortcut.
!   Subsequent packets flow spoke1 -> spoke2 directly over the NBMA network.
!
! NHRP parameters for this spoke:
!   NHS tunnel IP:  172.16.0.1    NHS NBMA IP:  10.0.0.1
!   Our tunnel IP:  172.16.0.11   Our NBMA IP:  10.0.0.11
! -------------------------------------------------------
!
hostname spoke1
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.11/32
!
interface Loopback1
   description Simulated LAN behind spoke1
   ip address 192.168.1.1/24
!
interface Ethernet1
   description WAN NBMA network (10.0.0.0/24)
   no switchport
   ip address 10.0.0.11/24
   no shutdown
!
interface Tunnel0
   description DMVPN mGRE tunnel
   tunnel source Ethernet1
   tunnel mode gre multipoint
   ip address 172.16.0.11/24
   no shutdown
   ! YOUR TASK: Add NHRP, OSPF broadcast (priority 0), ip nhrp shortcut (see hints above)
!
ip routing
!
end
